        "evidence_id": "pdfplumber:abstract",
        "source": "pdf_layout",
        "field": "abstract",
        "raw_text": "We present almost-optimal lattice-based attribute-based encryption (ABE) and laconic function evaluation (LFE). For depth d circuits over ℓ-bit inputs, we obtain - key-policy and ciphertext-policy ABE schemes with ciphertext, secret key and public key size O(1); - LFE with ciphertext size ℓ+ O( 1 )a sw e l la sC R Sa n dd i g e s ts i z e O(1); where O(·)h i d e spoly(d, λ) factors. Our parameter sizes are optimal, up to the poly(d) dependencies. The security of our schemes rely on succinct LWE (Wee, CRYPTO 2024). Our results constitute a substantial improvement over the state of the art; none of our results were known even under the stronger evasive LWE assumption.",
